on kernels, accepted to ACL 2026. This demonstrates how LLMs can be used to optimize and understand low-level performance-critical code, relevant to AI-assisted performance optimization.\",\n   300→    \"author\": \"Xing Ma, Yangjie Zhou, Wu Sun, et al.\",\n   301→    \"source\": \"ArXiv\",\n   302→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.05023\",\n   303→    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-07\",\n   304→    \"topics\": [\n   305→      \"LLM applications\",\n   306→      \"performance optimization\",\n   307→      \"attention mechanisms\",\n   308→      \"CUDA\",\n   309→      \"kernel optimization\",\n   310→      \"code understanding\"\n   311→    ],\n   312→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   313→  },\n   314→  {\n   315→    \"title\": \"The Impossibility Triangle of Long-Context Modeling\",\n   316→    \"description\": \"This paper (41 pages, 6 figures) explores fundamental trade-offs in long-context modeling for language models. As AI coding agents need to maintain increasingly large contexts (entire codebases, documentation, etc.), understanding these limitations is crucial for system design.\",\n   317→    \"author\": \"Yan Zhou\",\n   318→    \"source\": \"ArXiv\",\n   319→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.05066\",\n   320→    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-07\",\n   321→    \"topics\": [\n   322→      \"long-context modeling\",\n   323→      \"LLM limitations\",\n   324→      \"context windows\",\n   325→      \"theoretical constraints\",\n   326→      \"scaling laws\"\n   327→    ],\n   328→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   329→  },\n   330→  {\n   331→    \"title\": \"LCM: Lossless Context Management\",\n   332→    \"description\": \"A paper on lossless context management, addressing how to efficiently manage and compress context without losing information. Critical for AI coding agents that need to work with large codebases and maintain context across long sessions.\",\n   333→    \"author\": \"Clint Ehrlich, Theodore Blackman\",\n   334→    \"source\": \"ArXiv\",\n   335→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.04050\",\n   336→    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-07\",\n   337→    \"topics\": [\n   338→      \"context management\",\n   339→      \"compression\",\n   340→      \"LLM optimization\",\n   341→      \"memory efficiency\",\n   342→      \"context windows\"\n   343→    ],\n   344→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   345→  },\n   346→  {\n   347→    \"title\": \"KernelBench-X: A Comprehensive Benchmark for Evaluating LLM-Generated GPU Kernels\",\n   348→    \"description\": \"Introduces KernelBench-X, a benchmark for evaluating GPU kernels generated by LLMs. As AI coding agents are increasingly asked to write performance-critical code, having robust benchmarks for evaluating generated low-level code is essential.\",\n   349→    \"author\": \"Han Wang, Jintao Zhang, Kai Jiang, et al.\",\n   350→    \"source\": \"ArXiv\",\n   351→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.04956\",\n   352→    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-07\",\n   353→    \"topics\": [\n   354→      \"benchmarking\",\n   355→      \"LLM code generation\",\n   356→      \"GPU kernels\",\n   357→      \"performance evaluation\",\n   358→      \"CUDA\",\n   359→      \"code quality assessment\"\n   360→    ],\n   361→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   362→  },\n   363→  {\n   364→    \"title\": \"Adaptivity Under Realizability Constraints: Comparing In-Context and Agentic Learning\",\n   365→    \"description\": \"Compares in-context learning (what LLMs do naturally) with agentic learning (using tools and external systems). This distinction is fundamental to understanding when to use different approaches in AI coding systems.\",\n   366→    \"author\": \"Anastasis Kratsios, A. Martina Neuman, Philipp Petersen\",\n   367→    \"source\": \"ArXiv\",\n   368→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.04995\",\n   369→    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-07\",\n   370→    \"topics\": [\n   371→      \"in-context learning\",\n   372→      \"agentic learning\",\n   373→      \"learning theory\",\n   374→      \"adaptivity\",\n   375→      \"LLM capabilities\"\n   376→    ],\n   377→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   378→  },\n   379→  {\n   380→    \"title\": \"Vibe coding and agentic engineering are getting closer than I'd like\",\n   381→    \"description\": \"Simon Willison discusses how the line between 'vibe coding' (AI coding without understanding) and 'agentic engineering' (responsible AI-assisted development) is blurring. He realizes he's no longer reviewing every line of code Claude writes, treating AI agents like trusted external teams. Explores the normalization of deviance, new challenges in evaluating software quality, shifting bottlenecks in the development lifecycle, and why he's still not concerned for his career. Key insight: Real-world usage is now more valuable than test coverage when evaluating software.\",\n   382→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   383→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   384→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/6/vibe-coding-and-agentic-engineering/\",\n   385→    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-06\",\n   386→    \"topics\": [\n   387→      \"AI coding\",\n   388→      \"Claude Code\",\n   389→      \"vibe coding\",\n   390→      \"agentic engineering\",\n   391→      \"software engineering practices\",\n   392→      \"developer experience\"\n   393→    ],\n   394→    \"type\": \"opinion\"\n   395→  },\n   396→  {\n   397→    \"title\": \"Live blog: Code w/ Claude 2026\",\n   398→    \"description\": \"Simon Willison's live coverage of Anthropic's Code w/ Claude 2026 event. Key announcements: API volume up 17x YoY, increased rate limits for Claude Code (doubling for Pro/Max/Enterprise), SpaceX Colossus partnership for capacity, new Claude Managed Agent features (multi-agent orchestration, Outcomes, and 'Dreaming' for self-improvement), Claude Code Routines for async automation, CI auto-fix for PRs. Notable: Shopify and Mercado Libre targeting 90% autonomous coding by Q3 2026.\",\n   399→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   400→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   401→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/6/code-w-claude-2026/\",\n   402→    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-06\",\n   403→    \"topics\": [\n   404→      \"Anthropic\",\n   405→      \"Claude Code\",\n   406→      \"AI coding\",\n   407→      \"multi-agent systems\",\n   408→      \"developer tools\",\n   409→      \"product announcements\"\n   410→    ],\n   411→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   412→  }\n   413→]\n   414→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"
