      "content": "[\n  {\n    \"title\": \"Agents need control flow, not more prompts\",\n    \"description\": \"A Hacker News discussion (183 points) on a blog post arguing that AI agents need better control flow mechanisms rather than more prompting. This reflects a growing consensus in the AI coding community about the limitations of prompt-based approaches and the need for more structured agent architectures.\",\n    \"author\": \"bsuh (original author)\",\n    \"source\": \"Hacker News\",\n    \"url\": \"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=40611998\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-08\",\n    \"topics\": [\n      \"AI agents\",\n      \"control flow\",\n      \"prompt engineering\",\n      \"agent architecture\",\n      \"software design\"\n    ],\n    \"type\": \"discussion\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"Natural Language Autoencoders: Turning Claude's Thoughts into Text\",\n    \"description\": \"Anthropic research (91 points on HN) on natural language autoencoders that convert Claude's internal thoughts into text. This relates to making AI reasoning more interpretable, which is important for AI coding systems where understanding the model's reasoning process is valuable.\",\n    \"author\": \"Anthropic\",\n    \"source\": \"Hacker News\",\n    \"url\": \"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=40612145\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-08\",\n    \"topics\": [\n      \"Anthropic\",\n      \"interpretability\",\n      \"reasoning\",\n      \"autoencoders\",\n      \"Claude\",\n      \"AI research\"\n    ],\n    \"type\": \"discussion\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"AlphaEvolve: Gemini-powered coding agent scaling impact across fields\",\n    \"description\": \"Google DeepMind's AlphaEvolve (205 points on HN) showcases a Gemini-powered coding agent that scales its impact across multiple fields. This demonstrates the growing trend of domain-specific AI coding agents that can adapt to different programming domains.\",\n    \"author\": \"Google DeepMind\",\n    \"source\": \"Hacker News\",\n    \"url\": \"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=40612034\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-08\",\n    \"topics\": [\n      \"Google DeepMind\",\n      \"Gemini\",\n      \"coding agents\",\n      \"multi-domain AI\",\n      \"scaling\",\n      \"AI research\"\n    ],\n    \"type\": \"discussion\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"DeepSeek 4 Flash local inference engine for Metal\",\n    \"description\": \"A DeepSeek 4 Flash local inference engine for Metal (185 points on HN) by antirez. This enables efficient local running of DeepSeek models on Apple Silicon, relevant to developers who want to run AI coding models locally for privacy or performance reasons.\",\n    \"author\": \"antirez (Salvatore Sanfilippo)\",\n    \"source\": \"Hacker News\",\n    \"url\": \"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=40612078\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-08\",\n    \"topics\": [\n      \"DeepSeek\",\n      \"local inference\",\n      \"Metal\",\n      \"Apple Silicon\",\n      \"performance optimization\",\n      \"open source\"\n    ],\n    \"type\": \"discussion\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"Principles for agent-native CLIs\",\n    \"description\": \"Discussion (29 points on HN) about principles for building command-line interfaces that are native to AI agents. As AI coding agents become more prevalent, CLI tools need to be designed with agent interaction in mind, not just human interaction.\",\n    \"author\": \"trevin\",\n    \"source\": \"Hacker News\",\n    \"url\": \"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=40612251\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-08\",\n    \"topics\": [\n      \"CLI design\",\n      \"AI agents\",\n      \"developer tools\",\n      \"human-computer interaction\",\n      \"agent-native interfaces\"\n    ],\n    \"type\": \"discussion\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"Show HN: TRUST – Coding Rust like it's 1989\",\n    \"description\": \"A Show HN post (93 points) about TRUST, a Rust coding project. While not directly about AI coding, it reflects ongoing innovation in programming languages and tools that AI coding agents need to understand and work with.\",\n    \"author\": \"wojtczyk\",\n    \"source\": \"Hacker News\",\n    \"url\": \"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=40611901\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-08\",\n    \"topics\": [\n      \"Rust\",\n      \"programming languages\",\n      \"developer tools\",\n      \"Show HN\"\n    ],\n    \"type\": \"discussion\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"AI Slop Is Killing Online Communities\",\n    \"description\": \"A widely-discussed article (172 points on HN) about how AI-generated low-quality content ('slop') is damaging online communities. This raises important questions about the impact of AI coding tools on code quality and the software development ecosystem.\",\n    \"author\": \"rmoff\",\n    \"source\": \"Hacker News\",\n    \"url\": \"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=40611827\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-08\",\n    \"topics\": [\n      \"AI impact\",\n      \"online communities\",\n      \"content quality\",\n      \"social implications\",\n      \"AI ethics\"\n    ],\n    \"type\": \"discussion\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"ProgramBench: Can language models rebuild programs from scratch?\",\n    \"description\": \"An ArXiv paper discussed on HN (127 points) that benchmarks whether language models can rebuild programs from scratch. This is a relevant evaluation for AI coding agents, testing their ability to understand and recreate complete programs.\",\n    \"author\": \"Various researchers\",\n    \"source\": \"Hacker News\",\n    \"url\": \"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=40611795\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-08\",\n    \"topics\": [\n      \"benchmarking\",\n      \"LLM evaluation\",\n      \"program synthesis\",\n      \"code generation\",\n      \"AI research\"\n    ],\n    \"type\": \"discussion\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"ZAYA1-8B matches DeepSeek-R1 on math with less than 1B active parameters\",\n    \"description\": \"Discussion (72 points on HN) about ZAYA1-8B, a model that matches DeepSeek-R1 on math benchmarks with fewer than 1B active parameters. This reflects ongoing research into more efficient model architectures for AI coding and reasoning tasks.\",\n    \"author\": \"firethering.com\",\n    \"source\": \"Hacker News\",\n    \"url\": \"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=40612111\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-08\",\n    \"topics\": [\n      \"model efficiency\",\n      \"parameter optimization\",\n      \"math reasoning\",\n      \"DeepSeek\",\n      \"AI research\"\n    ],\n    \"type\": \"discussion\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"Show HN: Stage CLI – An easier way of reading your AI generated changes locally\",\n    \"description\": \"A Show HN post (24 points) about Stage CLI, a tool for reviewing AI-generated code changes locally. This addresses the growing need for better tools to review and understand code changes made by AI coding agents.\",\n    \"author\": \"cpan22\",\n    \"source\": \"Hacker News\",\n    \"url\": \"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=40612345\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-08\",\n    \"topics\": [\n      \"developer tools\",\n      \"code review\",\n      \"AI coding\",\n      \"CLI tools\",\n      \"Show HN\"\n    ],\n    \"type\": \"discussion\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"LongSeeker: Elastic Context Orchestration for Long-Horizon Search Agents\",\n    \"description\": \"A paper on elastic context orchestration for long-horizon search agents, addressing how to manage and optimize context windows for agents performing extended search tasks. Relevant to AI coding agents that need to maintain context over long sessions.\",\n    \"author\": \"Yijun Lu, Rui Ye, Yuwen Du, Jiajun Wang, Songhua Liu, Siheng Chen\",\n    \"source\": \"ArXiv\",\n    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.05191\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-07\",\n    \"topics\": [\n      \"AI agents\",\n      \"context management\",\n      \"search agents\",\n      \"long-horizon tasks\",\n      \"agent orchestration\"\n    ],\n    \"type\": \"technical\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"Executable World Models for ARC-AGI-3 in the Era of Coding Agents\",\n    \"description\": \"This paper explores executable world models for the ARC-AGI-3 benchmark, specifically in the context of coding agents. It addresses how AI agents can build and execute world models to solve complex reasoning tasks, relevant to the advancement of AI coding systems.\",\n    \"author\": \"Sergey Rodionov\",\n    \"source\": \"ArXiv\",\n    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.05138\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-07\",\n    \"topics\": [\n      \"AI agents\",\n      \"world models\",\n      \"ARC-AGI\",\n      \"coding agents\",\n      \"reasoning\",\n      \"benchmark evaluation\"\n    ],\n    \"type\": \"technical\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"Design Conductor 2.0: An agent builds a TurboQuant inference accelerator in 80 hours\",\n    \"description\": \"A remarkable case study where an AI agent built a complete TurboQuant inference accelerator in just 80 hours. This demonstrates the growing capability of AI agents to design complex hardware systems, with implications for AI-assisted hardware and system-level programming.\",\n    \"author\": \"The Verkor Team: Ravi Krishna, Suresh Krishna, David Chin\",\n    \"source\": \"ArXiv\",\n    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.05170\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-07\",\n    \"topics\": [\n      \"AI agents\",\n      \"hardware design\",\n      \"inference accelerators\",\n      \"TurboQuant\",\n      \"AI-assisted development\",\n      \"system design\"\n    ],\n    \"type\": \"technical\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"DecodingTrust-Agent Platform (DTap): A Controllable and Interactive Red-Teaming Platform for AI Agents\",\n    \"description\": \"A comprehensive 279-page paper introducing DTap, a platform for red-teaming AI agents. This addresses criti